# D15/T7d: a fixed array declared with ":=" from its constructor - the length is dropped (D15 says it declares
# Array<T, N>) and the value is copied into an Array<T> one element at a time in the IR (cgPromoteFixedToRuntimeLength):
# 100k elements take ~10s to compile (18MB of IR), 1M ~88s; 3,000,000,000 grew the compiler past 4.7GB until killed
fn main() ? {
    a := Array<U8, 100000>()
    a[5] = 7
    println($a.Len() " " $a[5])
}
